<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nagaland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1963</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nagaland is a state in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, bordering Myanmar, with its capital at Kohima. Inhabited mainly by Naga peoples, it became a separate state in 1963 after an armed Naga nationalist movement led by Angami Zapu Phizo had demanded independence since the 1950s. Kohima was the scene of a decisive battle against the Japanese in 1944, and talks with Naga insurgent groups have continued since a ceasefire in 1997.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nagaland.jpg" alt="Nagaland" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Suduvelu Rhakho · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kapamodzu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
